  "grantInterpretation": [
    "Public wrappers are SECURITY INVOKER; authenticated can execute with its verified session. The two private helpers are SECURITY DEFINER with a fixed search_path and explicit auth/tenant checks.",
    "authenticated has USAGE/EXECUTE needed inside SQL, not HTTP exposure of inbox_private. anon has neither.",
    "service_role retains default EXECUTE on public wrappers but has neither USAGE nor EXECUTE on inbox_private helpers; this does not establish an end-to-end service-role Inbox RPC contract.",
    "270 grants explicit safe settings columns to authenticated and backend read columns to service_role; select=* and explicit secret access fail closed for clients.",
    "269 protects profile administrative columns; 271 applies phone ownership and revokes two public cron RPCs; 272/273 restrict internal EXECUTE/TRUNCATE without compensation.",
    "graphql_public remains a configured schema. Existing GraphQL availability is not a new private helper endpoint; Postgres role/column grants still apply.",
    "graphql_public is configured but pg_graphql is not installed. Its existing invoker stub returns only an extension-not-enabled error; no GraphQL data service was enabled or tested."
  ],
  "compatibility": {
    "beforeRollout": "Old Inbox overloads exist; new wrappers do not. Do not promote candidate before 274.",
    "afterRollout": "New and retained historical Inbox consumers pass local SQL/Data API checks. The old settings/browser revalidation flow is intentionally incompatible after 270."
  },
